WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:02.080
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie.

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:06.490
This week for my Series 8 bonus video I wanted
to talk about all the new characters we’ve

00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:12.240
learned about so far there are about 12 total
but that number includes old characters coming

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:13.240
back.

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:17.830
There’s also been a lot of rumors about
the Master and Omega, but I’m going to focus

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:19.970
on the official people first.

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:23.189
If you’re finding me for the first time
I’m feeding out a steady diet of Doctor

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:27.449
Who videos while we wait for Series 8 to get
here.

00:00:27.449 --> 00:00:31.480
Be sure to subscribe to get everything and
feel free to leave me suggestions for videos

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:33.149
to do in the comments.

00:00:33.149 --> 00:00:34.550
So this is how I’m going to organize things.

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:39.649
I’ll talk about each new confirmed character
including Peter Capaldi and for each of them

00:00:39.649 --> 00:00:42.330
I’ll say what’s been confirmed then list
some of the bigger rumors.

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:48.329
Like for instance the rumor that Peter Capaldi
isn’t really playing The Doctor, he’s

00:00:48.329 --> 00:00:49.620
playing The Master in disguise.

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:55.920
I’m going to save details on the new episodes
for a separate video.

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:57.890
So let’s get started at the top

00:00:57.890 --> 00:01:02.300
Number 1 is Peter Capaldi as The 12th Doctor
or the 13th depending on how you count The

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:03.300
War Doctor.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:07.790
Here’s what’s been confirmed:
The BBC has announced Capaldi as The Doctor,

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:13.400
so barring any crazy plot twists he’ll complete
Series 8 with a regular Christmas Special.

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:16.890
There’s been no announcement as to Series
9, so we’ll have to wait to see if he stays

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:17.890
on.

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:21.259
There’s been a lot of talk about Moffat
departing whenever Capaldi departs.

00:01:21.259 --> 00:01:25.201
But tentatively let’s assume they’ll both
be here through Series 9 next year.

00:01:25.201 --> 00:01:32.810
Here are the big Capaldi Rumors: As I said
earlier, the biggest is that Capaldi really

00:01:32.810 --> 00:01:34.750
is only staying for one series because he’s
actually secretly playing The Master just

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:36.119
disguising himself as The Doctor.

00:01:36.119 --> 00:01:43.080
I think that’s rubbish just because we actually
saw the regeneration and the BBC specifically

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:48.329
said he was The Doctor.

00:01:48.329 --> 00:01:53.270
Number 2: Jenna Louise Coleman as Clara Oswald
She’s also only been confirmed through Series

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:56.020
8, no word on Series 9 yet.

00:01:56.020 --> 00:02:00.540
But primarily she’ll still have a warm relationship
with the new older Doctor.

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:05.490
Most of the on set pics of them show her in
generally good spirits.

00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:08.509
The only rumor I’ve heard about her is that
she’ll depart at the end of this series.

00:02:08.509 --> 00:02:11.110
I think it’s more likely that she’ll depart
when Capaldi departs.

00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:15.210
So that the next Doctor will start with completely
new companions, just like when Matt Smith

00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:16.990
became the new Doctor and he got Amy and Rory.

00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:19.330
Number 3: Samuel Anderson as Danny Pink

00:02:19.330 --> 00:02:24.330
A lot of sites are quoting him as a full on
companion, Rory style.

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:27.640
Like a companion that doesn’t board the
TARDIS right away, but later in the series

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:29.140
becomes more important.

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:33.481
Officially, the BBC has just called him a
new recurring character at Clara’s Coal

00:02:33.481 --> 00:02:34.710
Hill School.

00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:35.800
As another teacher.

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:40.480
Rumors: Here’s where it starts to get interesting,
there are so many people saying the Master

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:43.300
is coming back and just like in Series 3 with
Derek Jacobi.

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:46.780
Danny Pink is The Master in disguise.

00:02:46.780 --> 00:02:50.010
We haven’t seen any footage of him yet,
so until then it’s going to be harder to

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:54.160
guess what his character arc is and if he
in fact is pretending to be someone he’s

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:55.160
not.

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:56.510
Master or no Master.

00:02:56.510 --> 00:03:00.310
As for his relationship to Clara, I’m not
expecting him to be a love interest since

00:03:00.310 --> 00:03:02.040
that’s kind of been done to death.

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:06.340
Based on what the producers and cast are saying,
Series 8 is going to be much darker and more

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:10.580
serious than the relationship comedy Doctor
Who turned into during Matt Smith’s run.

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:14.970
That doesn’t mean there won’t be romance,
it just means the story won’t revolve around

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:15.970
love triangles.

00:03:15.970 --> 00:03:18.260
Number 4: Tony Way as Alfie

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:21.960
In case you don’t recognize him, he’s
playing Ser Dontos on Game of Thrones right

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:22.960
now.

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:24.040
Yay for crossovers.

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:26.650
In series 8 he’s appearing in Episode 1.

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:28.790
So he’ll be on right away once the series
starts.

00:03:28.790 --> 00:03:31.890
It’s not a huge part but it ties into the
Jack The Ripper plot.

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:36.590
There aren’t any big rumors for his character
since it’s just a one off guest spot.

00:03:36.590 --> 00:03:38.670
Number 5: Tom Riley as Robin Hood

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:43.570
This is part of the episode Mark Gatiss is
writing called Robots of Sherwood.

00:03:43.570 --> 00:03:47.130
So you can understand why Riley is called
Robin Hood.

00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:51.430
There were also a lot of pictures of Jenna
Louise Coleman wielding a bow and arrow in

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:54.220
a period costume too.

00:03:54.220 --> 00:03:59.230
No rumors other than the Robots in this episode
might be the Clockwork Droids from Girl in

00:03:59.230 --> 00:04:01.240
the Fireplace, since they’ve been rumored
to return.

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:03.850
Number 6: Ben Miller as an un-named Villain

00:04:03.850 --> 00:04:08.350
The episode he’s starring in is one of the
two that Mark Gatiss is writing, we know one

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:11.630
of those is the Robin Hood episode, but we
don’t know what the other is.

00:04:11.630 --> 00:04:14.970
Steven Moffat said that he would be playing
a “Storming good villain”.

00:04:14.970 --> 00:04:19.480
I don’t know if that’s meant to be taken
literally as in weather storm or figuratively

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:23.290
as in a storm of robots a la Robots of Sherwood.

00:04:23.290 --> 00:04:26.790
His casting annoucement was made the same
week as Tom Riley’s Robin Hood announcement

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:27.790
was made.

00:04:27.790 --> 00:04:30.570
So for now let’s assume Miller’s villain
will appear in the Sherwood episode.

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:32.910
Rumors: No real rumors about his character.

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:35.420
He’s only around for one episode, so I didn’t
pay any attention to talk about him being

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:36.420
The Master.

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:39.580
Everyone is so sure The Master is coming back,
every time the BBC says a new actor with a

00:04:39.580 --> 00:04:42.030
beard has been cast, people think it’s The
Master.

00:04:42.030 --> 00:04:44.400
Number 7: Robert Goodman as Reg

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:48.600
His character will appear in episode 4 with
a bunch of other guest actors that were announced

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:51.880
when Samuel Anderson was cast.

00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:56.880
Before Series 8, Goodman also starred on a
bunch of Doctor Who serials and played a monster

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:59.860
named Mandrel during the fourth Doctor’s
run.

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:02.250
No big rumors about him.

00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:09.340
Number 8: Jonathan Bailey and Pippa Bennett
Warner are also guest characters in episode

00:05:09.340 --> 00:05:11.300
4 but no info on who they’re playing.

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:17.400
Number 9: Keeley Hawes as Ms Delphox

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:19.050
We actually know a lot about her character.

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:25.090
She’ll be an evil banker and her episode
will take place in the distant future.

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:29.330
The big rumor is that because she’s such
an amazing actress, her character could secretly

00:05:29.330 --> 00:05:40.020
be the Rani or even a female Master.

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:42.100
Number 10: Michael Smiley as Colonel Blue

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:46.840
He’ll be starring in episode 2, the second
of Ben Wheatley’s two episodes.

00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:50.860
It seems like the episodes will be one big
story broken into two parts.

00:05:50.860 --> 00:05:54.301
So he’s probably someone who will be helping
The Doctor, Clara and the Paternoster gang

00:05:54.301 --> 00:05:58.500
solve the Jack The Ripper mystery that’s
rumored to be the basis for the story.

00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:04.390
and last group of people Number 11: The Paternoster
Gang and Paul Hickey as Inspector Gregson.

00:06:04.390 --> 00:06:08.910
Everyone knows Madame Vastra, Jenny and Strax,
but Paul Hickey’s Inspector Gregson character

00:06:08.910 --> 00:06:12.460
was last seen in The Snowmen the 2012 Christmas
Special.

00:06:12.460 --> 00:06:14.800
They’ll all be part of that first episode.

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:18.720
So that’s it for new characters so far.

00:06:18.720 --> 00:06:24.860
Neil Gaiman did say he was creating a new
monster and we know about the titles and directors

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:26.470
for 9 of the 13 episodes.

00:06:26.470 --> 00:06:28.070
But I’m going to save that for a future
video.

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:29.960
Be sure to subscribe to get it.

00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:33.140
Be sure to leave suggestions for bonus Doctor
Who videos you want to see me do.

00:06:33.140 --> 00:06:38.500
We still have a long long time before Series
8 premiere at the end of the summer.

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:41.260
I’m expecting it to start by August at the
latest.

00:06:41.260 --> 00:06:45.580
Also since a lot of you ask me about when
I’m posting videos just follow me on social,

00:06:45.580 --> 00:06:49.160
I usually give regular updates there.

